{"version":"2026-10-10T08:58:17.257Z","lang":"en","id":"013000701","slug":"md-sadique-reaz","nameBn":"Md Sadique Reaz","nameEn":"Md Sadique Reaz","photoUrl":"https://prp.parliament.gov.bd/api/files?_=MjAyNjAyMTQvcDIyMDE3NDA0X2M5NWM3NzZmOTZlOTQyMmE4YzBlMzhmYmE4ZjYxNDc1LmpwZw==","gender":"Male","party":"BNP","partyBn":"BNP","seatNo":7,"seatBn":"Dinajpur-2","seatSlug":"dinajpur-2","seatEn":"Dinajpur-2","districtBn":"Dinajpur","districtEn":"Dinajpur","districtSlug":"dinajpur","areaBn":"(ক)বোচাগঞ্জ এবং(খ) বিরল উপজেলা","officeBn":null,"reserved":false,"nameAlt":"মোঃ সাদিক রিয়াজ","seatAlt":"দিনাজপুর-২","districtAlt":"দিনাজপুর","professionBn":"Business","educationBn":"Master's degree in Commerce","birthPlaceBn":"Daula, Bochaganj, Dinajpur","dateOfBirth":"1965-12-20","fatherBn":null,"motherBn":null,"isFreedomFighter":false,"email":"dinajpur.2@parliament.gov.bd","bioBn":"Md Sadique Reaz (Sadique Reaz Chowdhury Pinak) is the member of parliament for Dinajpur-2 (Bochaganj and Birol) in the 13th Parliament. He has entered Parliament for the first time, from the Bangladesh Nationalist Party (BNP). He was born on 20 December 1965 in the village of Daula in Bochaganj upazila, Dinajpur district. His father is A F M Riazul Haque Chowdhury and his mother Suraiya Reaz. He holds a master's degree in commerce and is a businessman by profession.\n\nSadique Reaz has long been involved in politics in Dinajpur district. As an executive member of the district BNP he has played an active role in party activities. He was also the BNP's nominated candidate for Dinajpur-2 in the election to the 11th Parliament. In the election to the 13th Parliament held on 12 February 2026 he was elected MP, winning 139,622 votes with the sheaf of paddy symbol.","bioTranslated":true,"bioOnlyInBangla":false,"summaryBn":null,"summaryTranslated":false,"showSummary":false,"leadBn":"Md Sadique Reaz is a Bangladesh Nationalist Party member of the 13th Parliament elected from Dinajpur-2. This page gives his profile an